body:
> This one should fix it: [#69863](https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/69863) - but I do not think we will regenerate constraints/images for 3.3.0 - it will be fixed in 3.3.1 automatically.

@potiuk regenerate constraints/images for 3.3.0 might not be needed, I agree, it would be too much effort imo. I suggest/propose however to consider something like appending the release information for 3.3.0 with a warning mentioning the issue with the databricks provider 🤷

Just manually updating/setting `apache-airflow-providers-databricks==7.16.1` (is/was the latest release at the time of Airflow 3.3.0 release) or `apache-airflow-providers-databricks==7.15.0` (Airflow 3.2.2 release) solves the issue
